### Substitute-relevant summary

| Layer | What exists today |
|--------|-------------------|
| API | `PATCH learning-records/{id}/teacher` (director) + audit table `learning_record_teacher_changes` |
| `LearningRecord` | `TeacherID` on the record; optional `update_class` in controller updates `StudentClass.TeacherID` |
| `Schedule` | `teacher_id` on `schedules` rows (substitute at schedule level would be separate from LR patch) |
| `StudentSignIn` | `TeacherID` on attendance rows |
| CourseManagement UI | Course-level teacher via edit form; session chips open session edit **without** per-session teacher change |

If you want the parent agent to implement end-to-end substitute flow, the gaps are mainly: per-session / `ClassSession` / `schedules` teacher overrides, attendance `TeacherID` sync, and UI (chips or modal) to call the right APIs.

